The Atlas engine is built from Enntity/atlas at the commit in
install/atlas-source.json (AGPL-3.0-only).

The request and response shape follows TypeSafe AI's published System One API
(docs.typesafe.ai). SparkScore is not affiliated with TypeSafe AI. "Jev" is
TypeSafe AI's name for its model and is used here only to describe the API
shape and to compare results.

Model weights are not distributed here. Each checkpoint named in
install/checkpoints.json carries its authors' license.

tools/sparkscore reimplements, without copying code:
- the answer fields and confidence formulas of TypeSafe AI's
  system-one-adapter-python 0.2.1 (MIT);
- prompt-layout and label ideas from openjev-sglang (ekzhang), KnowLine
  (PelaAI, Apache-2.0), decider (Mapika, Apache-2.0) and SGLang's
  /v1/systemone (Apache-2.0), as credited in tools/sparkscore/templates/.
tools/sparkscore/templates/knowline_gen15.py is adapted from
knowline_layout.py and knowline_server.py of PelaAI/KnowLine-35B-A3B-Gen1.5
(huggingface.co/PelaAI/KnowLine-35B-A3B-Gen1.5, revision 9adcf717; the
repository is Apache-2.0; knowline_server.py says "Licence of this file:
MIT"). They credit llm2jev 0.6.1 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AnyJev contributors) for
the rendering and scoring code, OpenJev for the layout module, and FlexDM
(MIT) and RE2 (Xu et al., 2023) for the read-twice layout. Its tests compare
against those files, which are not included here.
tools/sparkscore/templates/d3_ultra.py is adapted from d3_format.py and
d3_runtime.py of vllm-sr/d3-ultra (Decision 3.0, Copyright 2026 vLLM Semantic
Router Team, Apache-2.0; huggingface.co/vllm-sr/d3-ultra, revision
ccdcfa61). Its tests compare against those files, which are not included
here.

The benchmark runners call Decision Index (MIT), JevBench (MIT) and kev
(Apache-2.0) from their own checkouts; none of their code is included here.
tools/sparkscore/bench/data/d3-bf16-reference.jsonl contains the text of
JevBench public items (MIT, Copyright (c) the JevBench authors,
github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench) as rendered by d3-ultra's runtime, with
d3-ultra's answers to them.

The demo pages (demo/) and the cards (docs/assets/cards.html) load Inter,
JetBrains Mono, Space Grotesk and Press Start 2P from Google Fonts (SIL Open
Font License 1.1); no font files are included.

tools/nvfp4_convert.py reproduces NVIDIA TensorRT Model Optimizer's (ModelOpt,
Apache-2.0) NVFP4 and FP8 weight quantization ("max" calibration) bit for bit,
written independently against nvidia/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 as the format
reference. No ModelOpt code is included.
